# Copy this file to .env (git-ignored, never committed) and fill in your own values.
# ./start.sh loads .env automatically before starting the engine.
#
# DEC-038 (2026-09-25, owner override of DEC-031/DEC-035's offline-only rule): everything below is
# OFF unless you set both TUNNELSCOPE_GENERATOR_BACKEND=cloud and an API key. With neither set, the
# tool runs exactly as it did before this decision: fully offline, no outside model.

# "local" (default, on-device, no network) or "cloud" (DEC-038: an outside model drafts remediation
# suggestions; the failing rule and the lab connection's current settings are sent to it, never a
# real capture or a real gateway; see tunnelscope/remediate/cloud_client.py for exactly what is sent).
# TUNNELSCOPE_GENERATOR_BACKEND=cloud

# Required if the backend above is "cloud". Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# TUNNELSCOPE_GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional: override the model (default: gemini-3.8-flash — the top reasoning model,
# gemini-3.1-pro-preview, returned 429 quota-exceeded on our own key's tier; measured 2026-09-25)
# TUNNELSCOPE_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash

# Also still required for ANY drafting UI to appear at all (local or cloud), unchanged from DEC-034:
# TUNNELSCOPE_GENERATOR=1
